  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize capturing Jacks and Queens early, as they are easier to 'snatch' than Kings and Aces. Keep your Rensho until you can capture a trick containing multiple face cards.\n\nRensho Timing: If your partner leads a plain suit and an opponent plays a King, that is the perfect time to play the Rensho to secure a high-value trick.\n\nBleeding the Deck: Like Bridge, lead trumps early to exhaust the opponents, then use your remaining long suits to walk home with the scoring face cards.",
